doc-number>0902424</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA"  created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9282661-A"  status="new"><document-id status="new"  format="epo"><country>JP</country> <doc-number>9282661</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit> <patcit ucid="US-5732062-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country> <doc-number>5732062</doc-number> <kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-5848043-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>5848043</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>N. NOBUKUNI ET AL.: 'Microstructural changes in GeSbTe film during repetitious overwriting in phase-change optical recording' J. APPL. PHYS. vol. 78, no. 12, 1995, pages 6980 - 6988, XP002930167</text><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1182649A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORIE MICHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI CHEM CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOBUKUNI NATSUKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIE, MICHIKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI CHEMICAL CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOBUKUNI, NATSUKO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORIE MICHIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOBUKUNI NATSUKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORIE, MICHIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOBUKUNI, NATSUKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Information subjected to mark length demodulation is recorded on a recording medium by recording marks with different mark lengths under the condition that the time length nT of one recording mark (T is a reference clock and shorter than 25 nsec, and n is a natural number of 2 or more) is given by nT = ( eta 1 +  alpha 1 +  beta 1 + ... +  alpha m +  beta m +  eta 2) T where m is the number of pulse division of 2 or more,  alpha i &gt; 0 (real number),  beta i &gt; 0 (real number),  beta m &gt;/= 0 (real number), -2 &lt;/=  eta 1 &lt;/= 2 (real number), -2 &lt;/=  eta 2 &lt;/= 2 (real number), and n/m &gt;/= 1.25, and a recording power is applied during a period  alpha iT and a bias power is applied during a period  beta iT.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Dans cette invention, les informations soumises à une démodulation par longueur des marques sont enregistrées sur un support d'enregistrement à l'aide de marques d'enregistrement présentant différentes durées de marques à condition que la durée nT d'une marque d'enregistrement (T est une horloge de référence plus courte que 25 nsec, et n est un nombre naturel égal ou supérieur à 2) satisfasse à l'équation nT = ( eta 1 +  alpha 1 +  beta 1 + ... +  alpha m +  beta m +  eta 2) T, m étant le nombre de division d'impulsion de 2 ou plus,  alpha i &gt; 0 (nombre réel),  beta i &gt; 0 (nombre réel),  beta m &gt;/= 0 (nombre réel), -2 &lt;/=  eta 1 &lt;/= 2 (nombre réel), -2 &lt;/=  eta 2 &lt;/= 2 (nombre réel), et n/m &gt;/= 1,25, une puissance d'enregistrement étant appliquée pendant une période  alpha iT et une puissance de polarisation étant appliquée pendant une période  beta iT.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>